export anchor KnittingPatternStyle:
    number: 108
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Knitting pattern
    idea: The dashboard reads like a printed knitting pattern, with row counters for numbers, yarn ball bands for projects, stitch charts for progress and pattern abbreviations for status.
    base: light
    palette:
        paper: #fdfcf8, the booklet page
        table: #ece9e1, behind the page
        charcoal: #2a2a2e, text, rules, stitch marks and the primary button
        chartGrid: #c9c6bd, chart cells and dotted rules, decoration only
        heatherBlue: #3d5a80, last week stitches and the focus halo
        rose: #a23e50, this week stitches, row labels, the progress marker, Behind and overdue
        moss: #4f6b3a, On track
        ochre: #8a5300, At risk
        counter: #e9e4d8, row counter bodies
        graphite: #5c5a55, meta and abbreviations
    type:
        Three stacks. Titles, labels and nav use Futura, Century Gothic,
        Avenir Next, Trebuchet MS. Text uses Charter, Bitstream Charter,
        Sitka Text, Cambria, Georgia. Counters, facts and abbreviations use
        ui-monospace, SF Mono, Menlo, Consolas. The title is 46px geometric
        500, counter digits 26px mono 600, band titles 19px geometric 600,
        section heads 13px geometric caps tracked 0.16em, body 16px serif
        at 1.55, facts 13px mono.
    layout:
        A white booklet page on a beige table with a soft shadow. A runner
        line holds a yarn ball logo, an underline search, a black Cast on a
        project button, a round outlined bell and a round MO. The nav is
        geometric caps over a double rule, Home bold with a rose underline.
        The title block reads Pattern of the week with the date in rose
        caps, Good morning, Mara, a line about six projects, and on the
        right a boxed gauge note with a crossed box and 4 tasks are overdue.
        A 300px left column shows Row counters, four barrel counters with
        three white digit windows each, 006, 023, 004 in rose, and 186,
        beside their labels, then an Abbreviations box defining ot, ar, bh,
        od, sts and co with their glyphs. The main column lists six yarn
        ball bands, each a white band with heathered diagonal yarn ends in
        its own colour, the name, a status pill, a mono line of Fibre, sts
        and co, and a 20 stitch chart row filled with V stitches to the
        percent and marked with a rose line. Chart A is a knitting chart
        grid with columns of V stitches, heather then rose, row numbers on
        the right and day letters below. Instructions so far lists the six
        activity items as Row 1 to Row 6.
    spacing: An 8px unit with a 10px stitch cell in charts. Page margins 48px.
    density: Medium high. Pattern like columns with small mono facts.
    corners: Square paper and bands. Round bell and avatar, pill status tags and soft 14px counter bodies.
    borders: 1.5px charcoal lines, a double rule under the nav and dotted grid rules between rows.
    shadows: Only the page lifts off the table with a soft shadow. Counters have a small inset lip.
    icons:
        Chart key glyphs at 12px. An open ring for On track, a solid
        triangle for At risk, a solid square for Behind and a crossed box for
        overdue, in a pill with the word.
    focus: A 2px charcoal outline offset 2px, a 5px paper gap and a 2px heather blue ring.
    tone: Pattern shorthand, such as sts 18 of 25, co 14 Nov, Row 3 and Cast on a project.
